@startuml lost-update
!include style.iuml
hide footbox

participant "Checkout A\n(NAIVE)" as A
database "store_inventory row\navailable = 1, reserved = 0" as DB
participant "Checkout B\n(NAIVE)" as B

A -> DB : SELECT available_qty
DB --> A : 1
B -> DB : SELECT available_qty
DB --> B : 1
note over A, B : Both see one unit left and pass the check in Java.
A -> DB : UPDATE SET available_qty = 0,\nreserved_qty = reserved_qty + 1
activate DB
note right of DB : A holds the row lock
B -> DB : UPDATE SET available_qty = 0,\nreserved_qty = reserved_qty + 1
note right of B : waits for A's lock
A -> DB : COMMIT
deactivate DB
DB --> B : lock granted; B writes the\nvalue it computed from its stale read
B -> DB : COMMIT
note over DB #FFE5E5
  available = 0, reserved = 2:
  two orders hold the same single unit (oversold).
  The lock only made B wait; it didn't make B re-check.
end note
@enduml
